@startuml
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing true
skinparam RoundCorner 8
skinparam ParticipantPadding 25
skinparam BoxPadding 15
skinparam maxMessageSize 235
skinparam DefaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam TitleFontSize 20
skinparam sequence {
    ArrowColor #555555
    ArrowFontName SansSerif
    ArrowFontSize 11
    LifeLineBorderColor #BDC3C7
    LifeLineBackgroundColor #ECF0F1
    ParticipantBorderColor transparent
    ParticipantBackgroundColor #34495E
    ParticipantFontName SansSerif
    ParticipantFontSize 13
    ParticipantFontColor white
    BoxBorderColor transparent
    BoxFontName SansSerif
    BoxFontSize 11
    BoxFontColor #6F8592
}
skinparam note {
    BackgroundColor #FFF9C4
    BorderColor #FBC02D
    FontName SansSerif
    FontSize 11
    FontColor #424242
}

title SkyPilot, Kueue and DSX: admission, attribution and logical job status

box "Separate SkyPilot API deployment" #EAF0FC
participant "SkyPilot API\ncluster and job control" as Sky
end box
box "Kubernetes control plane and node runtime" #EEF2F4
participant "Kubernetes API\nPods and Workloads" as API
participant "Kueue\nadmission controller" as Kueue
participant "Scheduler + Pod runtime\nplacement and execution" as Runtime
end box
box "Separate observation deployments" #E6F4ED
participant "DSX exporter\nPod roots and labels" as DSX
participant "kube-state-metrics\nWorkload conditions" as KSM
participant "UID adapter\nlab prototype only" as UID
end box
box "Proposed integration" #F4EDFC
participant "Sky API reader\nlogical associations" as Reader
end box
box "Monitoring" #FFF4DD
participant "Prometheus\nscrapes and joins" as Prom
end box

legend left
|= Arrow |= Meaning |
| <color:#555555>Solid gray</color> | Request, mutation or response |
| <color:#3274A1>Blue dashed</color> | Independent observation delivery |
| <color:#268354>Green</color> | Local evaluation or published metrics |
Actual lab behavior is shown outside the proposed Sky API reader branch.
The UID adapter is a tested lab prototype, not shipping DSX functionality.
endlegend

== A. Establish independent observations ==
DSX -> API: Establish metadata observations\nfor configured Pod scope
API --> DSX: Initial metadata and watch stream
Kueue -> API: List / watch managed Pods
API --> Kueue: Initial Pod objects and stream
KSM -> API: List / watch Kueue v1beta2 Workloads\nwith custom resource metric configuration
API --> KSM: Initial Workloads and stream
note over API,Prom
Each observer reads independently. This diagram shows one explanatory execution.
Watch delivery, reads and scrapes have no shared ordering or atomic snapshot.
end note

== B. Create two bare Pods; CPU quota is zero ==
[-> Sky: Launch a two-node task\nLocalQueue: research
Sky -> API: Create head and worker Pods\nshared SkyPilot cluster and Kueue group labels
API -> Kueue: Admission webhook for each Pod
Kueue --> API: Add admission and topology scheduling gates
API --> Sky: Pods persisted with UIDs p1 and p2\nphase Pending; no controller owner
note over Sky,Kueue
Both Pods use one group, train-a. Names and UIDs here are illustrative.
The lab ClusterQueue starts with nominal CPU quota 0.
end note

== C. Pending Pods already have DSX identity ==
par Kueue observes the Pod group
  API --[#3274A1]> Kueue: Independent Pod watch events
  Kueue -> API: Create group Workload w1\nordinary ownerReferences point TO p1 and p2
  API --> Kueue: Workload created\nownerReferences.controller=false
  Kueue -[#268354]> Kueue: Quota is insufficient\nkeep Pods gated; Admitted is false
else DSX observes the same Pods
  API --[#3274A1]> DSX: Independent Pod metadata events
  DSX -> DSX: Resolve controller-owner chain\nno owner: each Pod is its own root
  DSX -> API: Obtain full Pod objects for evaluation
  API --> DSX: Pod metadata, spec and status
  DSX -[#268354]> DSX: Evaluate Pod status and configured labelRules\nobject is the full Pod
  Prom -> DSX: Scrape /metrics
  DSX -[#268354]> Prom: dsx_workload_pod_info + Pending status\nPod UID and SkyPilot / Kueue labels
end
note over DSX,Prom
Pod attribution does not wait for admission, scheduling, or application start.
Adding labels changes query grouping. The DSX workload UID remains the Pod UID.
end note

== D. Raise CPU quota to 12; Kueue admits the group ==
[-> API: Lab operator changes nominal CPU quota\n0 -> 12
API --[#3274A1]> Kueue: Quota update observation
Kueue -[#268354]> Kueue: Reserve quota; satisfy admission and topology requirements
Kueue -> API: Mark Workload Admitted\nremove admission and topology gates
API --> Kueue: Updated Workload and Pods
API --[#3274A1]> Runtime: Ungated Pending Pods become schedulable
Runtime -> API: Bind Pods; report Running after containers start
API --> Runtime: Pod status accepted
API --[#3274A1]> DSX: Independent Pod changes
DSX -[#268354]> DSX: Refresh full objects; evaluate Running
note over Kueue,Runtime
Admission permits scheduling. It does not itself prove Running.
The quota values and both gate types were observed in the lab.
end note

== E. A SkyPilot job succeeds while its Pods remain Running ==
Sky -> Runtime: Run the task in existing cluster Pods
Runtime --> Sky: Task result: SUCCEEDED
Sky -[#268354]> Sky: Record logical job success
note over Sky,DSX
The cluster Pods continue Running after this job succeeds.
SkyPilot job status, Pod phase and Kueue Finished are distinct observations.
end note

== F. Join labels and Kueue conditions without changing roots ==
API --[#3274A1]> KSM: Independent Workload condition updates
KSM -[#268354]> KSM: Build Admitted / Finished condition gauges\ninclude namespace, group, Workload UID and reason
Prom -> KSM: Scrape configured custom resource metrics
KSM -[#268354]> Prom: kube_customresource_kueue_workload_condition
Prom -> DSX: Scrape current Pod identity and labels
DSX -[#268354]> Prom: dsx_workload_pod_info\nworkload_kind=Pod; workload_uid=Pod UID
Prom -[#268354]> Prom: Deduplicate valid Pod mappings\njoin conditions on cluster + namespace + group
note over KSM,Prom
The label join is current-state grouping by name, not immutable association.
Preserve cluster and namespace. Condition reason is not SkyPilot job status.
end note

== G. Optional reverse UID association: tested lab adapter ==
opt Separate read-only UID adapter, not shipping DSX
  UID -> API: Poll namespaced Workloads, then current Pods\nevery 2 seconds; bounded request timeouts
  API --> UID: Workload owner references and live Pod UIDs
  UID -[#268354]> UID: Index (namespace, live Pod UID) -> Workload UID\naccept ordinary owners; ignore retained old UIDs
  alt Exactly one Workload matches the live Pod UID
    Prom -> UID: Scrape /metrics
    UID -[#268354]> Prom: experimental_kueue_pod_info = 1\nPod UID + Workload UID
  else Missing or ambiguous match
    UID -[#268354]> UID: Omit association; report ambiguity when present
  end
  note over DSX,UID
This association is a separate metric. No ownerReferences are edited.
Existing DSX Pod roots and metrics remain unchanged.
  end note
end

== H. Optional logical job association: proposed integration ==
opt Proposed Sky API reader; not implemented in DSX
  Reader -> Sky: Poll job / service records and their clusters
  Sky --> Reader: Logical IDs, states and cluster relationships
  Reader -[#268354]> Reader: Scope identity to API instance\nlocal job identity also includes its cluster
  Reader -> API: Read the current Pods for those clusters
  API --> Reader: Pod UIDs and cluster labels
  Reader -[#268354]> Reader: Build proposed logical job -> Pod associations
  Prom -> Reader: Proposed scrape
  Reader -[#268354]> Prom: Proposed separate logical identity and job status metrics
  note over Reader,Prom #F3E8FF
Direct Sky API reads were tested. This integrated reader is a proposal.
Two concurrent jobs sharing a Pod cannot split that Pod's resource usage.
  end note
end

== I. Failed adapter reads clear only adapter associations ==
opt UID adapter receives a denied or failed Kubernetes read
  UID -> API: Poll Workloads or Pods
  API --> UID: Permission failure or request error
  UID -[#268354]> UID: Clear association and condition snapshot\ncollection_valid=0; log fixed diagnostic
  Prom -> UID: Scrape diagnostic state
  UID -[#268354]> Prom: No association series; collection_valid=0
  Prom -> DSX: Independent normal DSX scrape
  DSX -[#268354]> Prom: Existing Pod identity and status metrics
  note over DSX,Prom #FFE5E5
Failure is local to the optional adapter. It must not suppress DSX Pod metrics.
A later complete successful poll rebuilds the adapter snapshot.
  end note
end

== J. Delete a Pod; remove its current series ==
[-> API: Delete Pod p1 in the disposable lab
API --> API: Pod p1 no longer exists
par DSX receives deletion independently
  API --[#3274A1]> DSX: Pod deletion event
  DSX -[#268354]> DSX: Remove current Pod attribution / root series
else UID adapter completes its next successful poll
  UID -> API: Read Workloads and current Pods
  API --> UID: Live Pods exclude UID p1
  UID -[#268354]> UID: Remove p1 association\neven if Workload retains its old owner reference
end
Prom -> DSX: Next scrape has no deleted Pod series
Prom -> UID: Next successful adapter scrape has no p1 association
note over DSX,Prom
Prometheus retains historical samples. Current exporter series disappear.
A replacement Pod with the same name has a different UID and must be matched again.
end note
@enduml
